   "definition": {
    "extraction_status": "extracted",
    "value": "Within the common activated voxels, we associated brain function during both cues with dependence measures on both substances; a linear model was applied with contrast of smoking versus baseline as a dependent variable and age, gender, and ADS–loss of behavioral control as independent variables.",
    "value_source": "reported",
    "evidence": {
     "status": "present",
     "sets": [
      {
       "source": "model_quote",
       "spans": [
        {
         "text": "A linear model was applied with contrast of either alcohol versus baseline or smoking versus baseline as a dependent variable, and the independent variables included age, gender, and one behavioral assessment score from AUDIT, FTND, ADS, or ICS (or subcategories).",
